Requirements: 25   with obligations: 25

[task-01] When the review records, for each recorded way of failing and each candidate
    test, whether that test would fail if the delivered code contained that way of
    failing, it obtains a short reason only where the test would fail.
    -> record-failure-test-failure-matrix  [functional/explicit]
       The review records, for each recorded way of failing and each candidate test,
       whether that test would fail if the delivered code contained that way of failing.

[constraint-01] What the review obtains about a pair where the test would fail is which
    pair it is, that it would fail, and a short reason.
    -> pair-failure-reason-observable  [functional/explicit]
       For a pair where the test would fail, the review records which pair it is, that
       it would fail, and a short reason.

[constraint-02] What the review obtains about a pair where the test would not fail is
    which pair it is and that it would not fail, and nothing else.
    -> pair-not-fail-no-reason-and-nothing-else  [functional/explicit]
       For a pair where the test would not fail, the review records which pair it is and
       that it would not fail, with no reason.
    -> no-reason-on-not-fail-verdict  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-07)
       A verdict kept about a pair where the test would not fail carries no reason where
       it is stored.

[constraint-03] Which of the two an answer is, is settled by the verdict the answer
    carries, not by which fields happen to be present in it. An answer that reports the
    test would not fail and carries a reason anyway is not a verdict the review accepts.
    -> verdict-controls-reason-presence  [invariant/explicit]
       An answer's verdict determines whether it may carry a reason: an answer that
       reports the test would not fail must not include a reason, and an answer that
       reports the test would fail must include a reason.

[constraint-04] An answer that reports the test would fail and carries no reason is not
    a verdict the review accepts.
    -> fail-answer-needs-reason  [functional/explicit]
       An answer reporting that the test would fail includes a short reason.
    -> reject-fail-answer-without-reason  [error_handling/explicit]
       A verdict that reports the test would fail and carries no reason is not accepted.

[constraint-05] An answer the review does not accept leaves its pair recorded as
    unjudged, naming the way of failing, the test, and why, exactly as a pair the judge
    never answered about is.
    -> unjudged-on-rejection  [functional/explicit]
       A pair whose answer the review does not accept is recorded as unjudged, with the
       way of failing, the test, and the cause named.

[constraint-06] Both kinds of answer are asked for in the same request as each other.
    -> both-kinds-of-answer-in-same-request  [functional/explicit]
       Both kinds of answer are asked for in the same request as each other.

[constraint-07] A verdict the review keeps about a pair where the test would not fail
    carries no reason where it is stored.
    -> no-reason-on-not-fail-verdict  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-02)
       A verdict kept about a pair where the test would not fail carries no reason where
       it is stored.

[constraint-08] Which pairs the review judges is unchanged.
    -> pairing-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       The set of pairs the review judges is unchanged.

[constraint-09] When the review reuses a verdict rather than producing it again is
    unchanged.
    -> pair-selection-stability  [invariant/explicit]
       The set of pairs the review judges stays unchanged when it reuses a verdict
       rather than producing it again.

[constraint-10] When the review produces a verdict again rather than reusing it is
    unchanged.
    -> reuse-verdict-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       The review's decision to produce a verdict again rather than reuse an existing
       verdict is unchanged.

[constraint-11] Whether the review reports the work complete, every rating it gives a
    criterion, and every test it recommends are unchanged.
    -> preserve-completion-ratings-and-test-recommendations  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve whether the review reports the work complete, every rating it gives a
       criterion, and every test it recommends.

[exclusion-01] Which ways of failing the review records, and how it produces them.
    -> no-recording-failure-ways-or-production-method  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which ways of failing the review records or how it
       produces them.

[exclusion-02] Deriving a criterion's rating, the completion conclusion, or any
    recommended test from judged pairs.
    -> no-deriving-ratings-completion-or-tests-from-judged-pairs  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not derive a criterion's rating, the completion conclusion, or
       any recommended test from judged pairs.

[exclusion-03] What the review shows a reader about a pair it has judged.
    -> show-reader-judged-pair  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter what the review shows a reader about a pair it has
       judged.

[exclusion-04] How pairs are grouped into requests, and the limit on how many judgements
    one request asks for.
    -> request-grouping-and-judgement-limit-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter how pairs are grouped into requests or the maximum
       number of judgements a request asks for.

[exclusion-05] Running the delivered code or any test.
    -> no-running-delivered-code-or-tests  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not involve running the delivered code or any test.

[completion-01] Implementation.
    -> implementation  [docs_config/explicit]
       Implementation.

[completion-02] A test reads the shape of the request as it is sent and fails if that
    shape permits a reason on a pair where the test would not fail.
    -> request-shape-rejects-spurious-reason  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test reads the shape of the request as it is sent and fails if that shape
       permits a reason on a pair where the test would not fail.

[completion-03] A test fails when an answer reporting that the test would fail carries
    no reason and is nonetheless kept as a verdict.
    -> test-fails-on-missing-reason-for-failing-answer  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test fails when an answer reporting that the test would fail carries no reason
       and is nonetheless kept as a verdict.

[completion-04] A test fails when an answer reporting that the test would not fail
    carries a reason and is nonetheless kept as a verdict.
    -> test-fails-on-reason-for-not-fail-verdict  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test fails when an answer reporting that the test would not fail carries a
       reason and is nonetheless kept as a verdict.

[completion-05] A test asserts that a pair whose answer the review does not accept is
    recorded as unjudged, naming the way of failing, the test and the cause.
    -> unjudged-on-rejected-answer  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a pair whose answer the review does not accept is recorded as
       unjudged, naming the way of failing, the test and the cause.

[completion-06] A test asserts that a stored verdict about a pair where the test would
    not fail carries no reason.
    -> stored-verdict-no-reason  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a stored verdict about a pair where the test would not fail
       carries no reason.

[completion-07] A test asserts that adding one candidate test between two continued runs
    produces new verdicts only for pairs concerning that test.
    -> new-verdicts-only-for-new-test  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that adding one candidate test between two continued runs produces
       new verdicts only for pairs concerning that test.

[completion-08] Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review
    state and byte-identical report output.
    -> deterministic-recorded-runs  [regression/explicit]
       Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review state and
       byte-identical report output.
